(6501509, 965324, 136346, '<td valign="top">IMO there is nothing bad with this photo, it is simply great - technically, compositionally, and content-ually.</td>', 'IMO there is nothing bad with this photo, it is simply great - technically, compositionally, and content-ually.', '2011-08-11 08:29:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6501521, 966435, 53147, '<td valign="top">Hey Steve. I gave this a 7 in challenge. I think this image has a cool feel to it. The light works well on your model and the scenery. Good shadows and grain. What my eye desires from a composition perspective is a bit more space on the left hand side. Maybe enough to have the light centered up top. That may have allowed the full shadow of your model to play out in the scene and offer up an even darker image. Overall though a good image for this challenge IMO.</td>', 'Hey Steve. I gave this a 7 in challenge. I think this image has a cool feel to it. The light works well on your model and the scenery. Good shadows and grain. What my eye desires from a composition perspective is a bit more space on the left hand side. Maybe enough to have the light centered up top. That may have allowed the full shadow of your model to play out in the scene and offer up an even darker image. Overall though a good image for this challenge IMO.', '2011-08-11 08:49:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6501525, 966396, 114233, '<td valign="top">I havent been through all the entries yet but this one caught my eye straight away. Yes it could be argued that this isnt Film Noir-ish enough but:<br/>Composition - Couldnt ask for better. I dont mind that he (you I guess) is looking out of the frame rather than into it. All major elements are on a thirds line or close enough. <br/>Technique - you certainly know how to use and control lighting. There is just enough light to accentuate the key areas and give shape to objects. The hair / shoulder light at the back is a nice touch as is the focused light on the cigar / bottom lip. (Is that a skull in the reflection of the glasses? :-) Protagonist''s death?! - see it does fit the challenge well!)<br/>PP - I love this look and you have controlled it very well. My only nit would be to use an off white line in the letter box border - the white is a bit too bright compared to the rest of the image... perhaps the same tone as the tip of his nose? Just a thought.<br/>Overall - maybe not what the viewers consider a film noiresque shot but a fine shot none the less!</td>', 'I havent been through all the entries yet but this one caught my eye straight away. Yes it could be argued that this isnt Film Noir-ish enough but:Composition - Couldnt ask for better. I dont mind that he (you I guess) is looking out of the frame rather than into it. All major elements are on a thirds line or close enough. Technique - you certainly know how to use and control lighting. There is just enough light to accentuate the key areas and give shape to objects. The hair / shoulder light at the back is a nice touch as is the focused light on the cigar / bottom lip. (Is that a skull in the reflection of the glasses? :-) Protagonist''s death?! - see it does fit the challenge well!)PP - I love this look and you have controlled it very well. My only nit would be to use an off white line in the letter box border - the white is a bit too bright compared to the rest of the image... perhaps the same tone as the tip of his nose? Just a thought.Overall - maybe not what the viewers consider a film noiresque shot but a fine shot none the less!', '2011-08-11 09:13:03.000000', NULL, 1),
