(6507492, 966443, 130147, '<td valign="top"><br/>CrazyDiamond, to answer your question about the shadows on the background. I tried lots of stuff to get the shadow but didn''t have enough room to cast such a big shadow. So I made it from a 50cmx50cm black cardboard and taped it to a lightstand. Then I put it in front of the camera and marked on the floor were the lightstand should be. Took it away and took the picture, then moved the lightstand were i had marked and manually shot a speedlite. Hench the 30 sec exposure.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-08-17 16:24:15.</i></td>', 'CrazyDiamond, to answer your question about the shadows on the background. I tried lots of stuff to get the shadow but didn''t have enough room to cast such a big shadow. So I made it from a 50cmx50cm black cardboard and taped it to a lightstand. Then I put it in front of the camera and marked on the floor were the lightstand should be. Took it away and took the picture, then moved the lightstand were i had marked and manually shot a speedlite. Hench the 30 sec exposure.', '2011-08-17 17:23:15.000000', '2011-08-17 17:24:15.000000', 0),
