(6508126, 966425, 114233, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by josephtagle:</b></div><hr/><i> Wow Super great, my very first ribbon, tnx for the red. <br/>I would like to especially acknowledge the whole team(Freedomwall) for another successful shoot.<br/>Thank you Paolo for the lovely make-up, it works all the time, tnx for sharing your talent.<br/>Thanks also to Fath, for being such a Film Noir model, very effective modeling as always.<br/>To Gerald tnx for being our lightman for the day.Tnx for the strobes bro.<br/> <br/>The set up was not my style (strobing) but it worked real fine (i think I should consider strobing on my other shoots, hmmmmm). I have one strobe set up behind a DIY window blind(made by Paolo), and 2 continuous light as backlight behind Fath, one to have some light on the background and one directly pointed to Fath.<br/> <br/>And thank you guys for all the inspiring comments, and for appreciating the photo, the model, the make up the styling and for believing that the photo will have a ribbon.<br/> <br/>Tnx DPCHALLENGE for having such photo contest, without the guys behind the contest this wont be possible. so Rock On guys!!!! <br/> <br/>Keep shooting.. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Certainly a fantastic shot and well deserving of a ribbon!<br/>Just wish your average vote given out was a bit higher...</td>', 'Originally posted by josephtagle: Wow Super great, my very first ribbon, tnx for the red. I would like to especially acknowledge the whole team(Freedomwall) for another successful shoot.Thank you Paolo for the lovely make-up, it works all the time, tnx for sharing your talent.Thanks also to Fath, for being such a Film Noir model, very effective modeling as always.To Gerald tnx for being our lightman for the day.Tnx for the strobes bro. The set up was not my style (strobing) but it worked real fine (i think I should consider strobing on my other shoots, hmmmmm). I have one strobe set up behind a DIY window blind(made by Paolo), and 2 continuous light as backlight behind Fath, one to have some light on the background and one directly pointed to Fath. And thank you guys for all the inspiring comments, and for appreciating the photo, the model, the make up the styling and for believing that the photo will have a ribbon. Tnx DPCHALLENGE for having such photo contest, without the guys behind the contest this wont be possible. so Rock On guys!!!!  Keep shooting..  Certainly a fantastic shot and well deserving of a ribbon!Just wish your average vote given out was a bit higher...', '2011-08-18 09:19:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6508148, 965823, 12611, '<td valign="top">I like the softness; it works here; nice mood created with the smoke- if he was staring down it might work better; or perhaps off into the middle distance, it loses some mystique and feel with the eyes aware of the camera.</td>', 'I like the softness; it works here; nice mood created with the smoke- if he was staring down it might work better; or perhaps off into the middle distance, it loses some mystique and feel with the eyes aware of the camera.', '2011-08-18 09:39:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6508155, 966295, 12611, '<td valign="top">Great set up and execution- This seems underrated for sure. I think I know why; the challenge calls for a dark or quirky shot a la the film genre; the hat the guy is wearing is too small to be taken seriously, and therefore, the mystique is out of the shot, its not so far as to be comical, but  just a lot less serious.</td>', 'Great set up and execution- This seems underrated for sure. I think I know why; the challenge calls for a dark or quirky shot a la the film genre; the hat the guy is wearing is too small to be taken seriously, and therefore, the mystique is out of the shot, its not so far as to be comical, but  just a lot less serious.', '2011-08-18 09:42:42.000000', NULL, 0),
